e":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet Sub-Committee (Local Authority Trading Companies' Shareholder)","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"North Hertfordshire capital plan hit by \u00a34.4m backlog and \u00a33m funding loss","lead":"North Hertfordshire's capital spending plan for 2026/27 has been disrupted by project delays and a significant loss of planned funding. The capital programme is forecast at \u00a313.57m, but \u00a34.4m represents slippage from 2025/26 \u2014 projects originally scheduled for last year that remain incomplete. The council also expected \u00a33m from selling assets, but a review by the estates team has eliminated this funding source: one site will be let rather than sold, and two others cannot be disposed of while securing best value. The loss forces increased internal borrowing \u2014 using the council's own cash reserves instead of loans \u2014 which will increase the minimum revenue provision, money set aside annually for repayment, in future years. Cabinet noted the capital programme requires close monitoring for affordability.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"6B - FAR - First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32129/32129.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"North Hertfordshire capital spending hampered by project delays and failed asset sales","lead":"North Hertfordshire Council faces mounting pressure on its ability to deliver building and infrastructure projects after delays and changes to its funding plans. The capital programme for 2026/27 has swollen to \u00a313.6m, but \u00a34.4m of this is spending that slipped from the previous year. More significantly, the council expected to raise \u00a33m from selling assets but a review by its estates team found that one site will be let rather than sold and two others cannot be disposed of this year without accepting lower prices. The shortfall forces the council to use its own cash reserves to pay for projects instead of borrowing, a strategy that depletes its financial cushion and increases future costs. Cabinet approved a \u00a30.67m addition to the 2027/28 capital programme but noted that the programme must be kept under review for affordability.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"6B - FAR - First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32129/32129.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","headline":"Planned service desk development efficiency no longer achievable as work shifts from in-house development to external procurement.","detail":"Planned ongoing efficiency saving of \u00a325k from in-house development of new service desk solution will not be achieved. Originally intended as internal development project to deliver efficiency, but due to its complexity and technical resources being absorbed by LGR support requirements, system must now be procured externally. External procurement deferred to next financial year with \u00a325k carry forward requested. Ongoing annual support and maintenance costs also expected to be significantly higher than estimated as market has moved away from locally hosted software to subscription-based cloud platforms (\u00a344k estimated 2027/28 impact).","category":"savings","matters":"Planned efficiency not being delivered due to resource constraints and technical complexity; external procurement costs higher than originally assumed.","figures":"\u00a325k planned efficiency not achieved, \u00a325k carry forward, \u00a344k estimated 2027/28 impact","quote":"The planned ongoing saving from the service desk being developed in house will not be achieved, as explained in table three above. \u00a325k underachievement.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","headline":"Thomas Bellamy House future use uncertain; lettings income delayed indefinitely to Autumn 2027 at earliest.","detail":"Future use of Thomas Bellamy House property remains uncertain. Options appraisal expected to be completed in current year to consider potential letting arrangements, capital expenditure requirements, and potential capital receipt from sale. No income anticipated prior to Autumn 2027 at earliest pending completion of appraisal and subsequent decisions. Creates \u00a337k current year budget shortfall and estimated \u00a319k impact on 2027/28.","category":"income","matters":"Budgeted property letting income deferred indefinitely; property disposition strategy unclear creating multi-year revenue uncertainty.","figures":"\u00a337k current year shortfall, \u00a319k estimated 2027/28 impact","quote":"The future use of Thomas Bellamy House remains uncertain... Income from letting would not be anticipated prior to Autumn 2027 at the earliest, pending the outcome of the appraisal and subsequent decisions.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","headline":"Solar for Business Initiative project closed without completing any installations, losing \u00a321k planned efficiency.","detail":"Solar for Business Initiative was intended to generate income and deliver \u00a321k efficiency saving but project has closed without any installations being completed due to difficulties attracting suitable business interest. Scheme has generated no income and efficiency has not been achieved, creating \u00a321k contribution to overall efficiency shortfall of \u00a359k in quarter one.","category":"savings","matters":"Planned efficiency not being delivered; market did not develop as anticipated for this income/savings opportunity.","figures":"\u00a321k planned efficiency lost","quote":"This project was closed without any installations being completed, due to difficulties in attracting suitable business interest. As a result, the scheme has not generated any income.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","headline":"Multiple capital and digital projects deferred or paused, primarily citing Local Government Reorganisation uncertainty.","detail":"Careline call handling system procurement deferred to March 2027 completion (implementation costs now expected in 2027/28). Careline service desk solution carry forward requested for 2027/28 due to complexity and technical resources absorbed by LGR support requirements. Agile AI procurement paused following Hertfordshire County Council decision not to lead and other councils' collaboration not progressing due to LGR. Idox Insights installation deferred pending LGR decisions. Royston Town Council Annexe redevelopment delayed awaiting access resolution and car park renewal with HCC. Total of approximately \u00a394k requested carry forwards plus other deferred strategic investments.","category":"capital","matters":"Multiple strategic project deferrals indicate substantial LGR uncertainty affecting investment and service delivery planning across multiple directorates.","figures":"\u00a325k Careline service desk carry forward, \u00a334k Careline call handling carry forward, \u00a345k planning software carry forward, \u00a320k Royston annexe carry forward","quote":"Progress with the procurement of Agile AI has however been paused in the new financial year following the Hertfordshire County Council decision not to lead on the procurement and the subsequent collaboration with other Councils not progressing due to LGR.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","headline":"Business rates collection forecast below government's baseline assessment but protected by one-year only 100% safety net.","detail":"Reset of business rates retention system on 1 April 2026 updated council's baseline. Council currently expects to collect less business rates income than the Baseline Rates by Baseline, which would normally leave it below baseline funding level. However, government has set safety net at 100% of baseline funding level for 2026/27 only (normally 92.5%), providing \u00a3432k top-up funding. This protection expires after 2026/27, creating funding vulnerability for 2027/28 and beyond.","category":"income","matters":"Business rates funding below government's assessed need for the council; temporary protection expires next year, creating funding risk.","figures":"100% safety net (normally 92.5%), \u00a3432k safety net funding for 2026/27 only","quote":"for 2026/27 only the government has set the safety net at 100%. Based on the forecast business rates position declared to Government in January, the Council will receive \u00a3432k of safety net funding in 2026/27.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"North Hertfordshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Planned service desk development efficiency no longer achievable as work shifts from in-house development to external procurement.","lead":"Planned efficiency not being delivered due to resource constraints and technical complexity; external procurement costs higher than originally assumed.","also":["53 other findings in this window","1 paper caught"],"watch":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-11-10","n_findings":54,"n_documents":1,"top_paper_title":"First Quarter Revenue Budget Monitoring 2026/27","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.north-herts.gov.uk/documents/s32097/32097.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":128,"news_drafts_total":2}}